# homeDX Platform Context

- Treat this repo as the full homeDX platform. The active app is `backend/` plus `frontend/mobile/hdx_mobile/`. Cube SDK reference lives under `vendor/` (local/gitignored binaries); the Android AAR used at build time is in `frontend/mobile/hdx_mobile/android/app/libs/`. `flutter/` is a local Flutter SDK checkout if present — avoid editing unless the user explicitly targets it. Non-code project work (market, meetings, roadmap, partnerships, brand, finance, notes, etc.) lives in `work/` (see `.cursor/rules/homedx-work.mdc` when those files are in play).
- Backend: NestJS 11 + TypeScript + Prisma/PostgreSQL. Entry points are `backend/src/main.ts` and `backend/src/app.module.ts`; it listens on `0.0.0.0:4000`. The Flutter-compatible REST API is the `mobile-*.controller.ts` set under `/gg-homedx-json/gg-api/v1`.
- Backend domains include auth/users, rapid tests, Cube result submission, payments (Stripe/PayPal), test kits, certificates, audit logs, notifications, legal pages, and file uploads. Prisma models live in `backend/prisma/schema.prisma`.
- Mobile app: Flutter/Dart in `frontend/mobile/hdx_mobile/`, using Provider, GoRouter, `flutter_dotenv`, `shared_preferences`, HTTP REST, Bluetooth, Stripe, and PayPal WebView. App startup wires services/providers in `lib/main.dart`; routes are in `lib/config/app_router.dart`; app constants and API base URL are in `lib/core/constants.dart`.
- Mobile API pattern: use `ApiService` (`lib/core/api_service.dart`) for REST calls to `AppConstants.apiBaseUrl + AppConstants.apiPath` (`/gg-homedx-json/gg-api/v1`). Auth stores JWT in shared preferences and sends both `Authorization: Bearer <token>` and `x-auth-token` where applicable.
- Cube integration: Flutter `lib/features/cube/cube_service.dart` talks to Android native `CubeBridge` in `android/app/src/main/kotlin/com/homedx/app/CubeAnalysisMethodChannel.kt` via MethodChannel `com.homedx.cube/analysis` and EventChannel `com.homedx.cube/events`. Android `applicationId`/`namespace` is `com.homedx.app`. The native Cube SDK scans Cube devices, connects, evaluates on-device, reads measurement results, then Flutter submits normalized results to backend `submit-cube-data`.
- Cube pairing: if Android asks for a PIN/passkey, use the last six digits of the Cube serial number. The test flow is phone Bluetooth -> Cube SDK measurement -> Flutter reads results -> backend stores a `RapidTest` -> app displays results.
- WSL2 networking: backend should be reachable on port 4000. For a physical phone, set `frontend/mobile/hdx_mobile/.env` to `API_BASE_URL=http://<Windows-LAN-IP>:4000` using the Windows LAN IPv4, not the WSL IP. Re-run `scripts/wsl/setup-wsl-port-forward.cmd` as Admin after WSL restarts; `scripts/wsl/check-homedx-connectivity.ps1 -UpdateMobileEnv` can sync the mobile `.env`.
- Common commands: root `./deploy.sh all|backend|mobile`, `./stop.sh`; WSL helpers under `scripts/wsl/`; backend `npm run start:dev`, `npm run lint`, `npm test`; Flutter app `flutter pub get`, `flutter analyze`, `flutter test`, `flutter run`.
- **After Flutter/mobile UI changes:** always rebuild web, restart the dev servers, and tell the user to hard refresh:
  1. `cd frontend/mobile/hdx_mobile && flutter build web --release`
  2. `fuser -k 8080/tcp; ./serve-web.sh 8080` (SPA-aware; do not use plain `python3 -m http.server`)
  3. Ensure Postgres (`docker start hdx-postgres`) and backend are up (`cd backend && npm run start:dev` on port 4000)
  4. Open `http://127.0.0.1:8080` (not `localhost` — IPv6 mismatch on WSL2). Hard refresh (Ctrl+Shift+R).
  `.env` should use `API_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:4000`. On WSL2 + Windows browser, remove stale `netsh` portproxy on 4000 if API calls fail (see `docs/WSL2_PORT_FORWARDING.md`).
- Testing expectations: backend has a Jest e2e smoke test at `backend/test/app.e2e-spec.ts`; Flutter has widget tests under `frontend/mobile/hdx_mobile/test/`. For Cube changes, manual E2E requires a real Android device and Cube: connect/pair, scan in-app, start a test, verify backend submission and displayed result.
- Regulatory context: homeDX is an accessory to the Cube IVD/medical device and is in scope for EU MDR/IVDR and German MPDG. Before touching `RapidTest` result logic, Cube data parsing, certificates, or health-data handling, read `.cursor/rules/mdr-compliance.mdc`.
